cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or parts of its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NDM Linux Backup"
abstract: >-
  A single Bash script for system backup and disaster recovery on Debian/GNU Linux. It
  saves the parts of a machine that most backup tools leave out (hardware information,
  UEFI/BIOS/MBR, partition tables, LUKS headers, LVM, installed packages, crontabs,
  database schemas, Docker/Podman configuration) into a settings archive, with optional
  separate data and secrets archives, GPG encryption and retention.
